- ### Molecules
+ ### Moléculas

- Atoms are bonded into a molecule with `*`, and an atom which is repeated takes its number as
- a type argument. A molecule is written out with proper subscripts:
+ Los átomos se enlazan en una molécula con `*`, y un átomo repetido toma su número como argumento
+ de tipo. Una molécula se escribe con los subíndices adecuados:

= a type argument. A molecule is written out with proper subscripts:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- val water = H[2]*O
+ val water = H[2]*O

= val water = H[2]*O
- ```
+ ```

= val water = H[2]*O
= ```
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= val water = H[2]*O
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= val water = H[2]*O
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
